                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                        "entry_id": "8e70b95c-177c-3ede-ab86-e208124d80b4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. тот, кто недавно приступил к обучению, вступил в какую-либо должность, общество; новичок"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "74f36888-6db2-4f37-8f2e-5dcf0bd6440d",
                                "sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                                "text": "За несколько месяцев до смерти своего родителя князь Андрей Юрьевич Шелешпанский поступил из недорослей в московское укилецкое войско новиком."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd41c3d2-84f6-4b62-8c99-9624c127013f",
                                "sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                                "text": "Мой сын всё досмотрит: он на всех хитрощах весьма зналый и дошлый. Я нарочито и дал его твоему новику для опеки и догляда."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60bae49a-0f72-4d14-94c0-a944ad0d2c38",
                                "sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                                "text": "Нащокин был чужой среди московского служебного мира и как политический новик должен был с бою брать свое служебное положение, чувствуя, что каждый его шаг вперед увеличивает число его врагов, особенно среди московской боярской знати."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b2e80bfa-2e12-4b01-bf85-9b45489498ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e70b95c-177c-3ede-ab86-e208124d80b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                        "target_lang_word": "beginner",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beginner",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6964d3b-343d-3efb-8370-cba28f0b648d",
                                        "entry_id": "48850c69-9a72-35b9-af4e-77e1a8f28ad1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who is just starting at something, or has only recently started."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2659f72-b8f4-4e69-bb4e-8524650cdb3d",
                                                "sense_id": "d6964d3b-343d-3efb-8370-cba28f0b648d",
                                                "text": "I'm new to learning Finnish: I'm just a beginner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6c149e1-d89f-38ab-847e-21ad27ca3b57",
                                        "entry_id": "48850c69-9a72-35b9-af4e-77e1a8f28ad1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who sets something in motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6dea45a-6542-4e46-b1d5-6ae6eaee2827",
                                                "sense_id": "d6c149e1-d89f-38ab-847e-21ad27ca3b57",
                                                "text": "The beginner of the games lit the ceremonial torch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c342247e-4537-3755-9ba4-9b4ca98a3579",
                                        "entry_id": "48850c69-9a72-35b9-af4e-77e1a8f28ad1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An actor who is present on stage in the first moments of a play."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41ffbc85-419c-4977-893d-f818881e997d",
                                                "sense_id": "c342247e-4537-3755-9ba4-9b4ca98a3579",
                                                "text": "On the stage, the beginners for the first piece had taken their places — the chorus were there, scared but determined, and in the wings waited Harlequin, in the person of Charles Lyall […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4bfb8bce-975e-4eab-a6d1-49aa841e4c7a",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e70b95c-177c-3ede-ab86-e208124d80b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "53ac8c69-1e23-3c32-bfff-78feb29cd488",
                        "target_lang_word": "newcomer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "newcomer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e95bf882-c189-3b0d-b750-d69f880c9de3",
                                        "entry_id": "32ab7118-4cd3-3fd5-b7f8-e5ec8827d7ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who has recently come to a community; a recent arrival."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b3a4816-bd1b-4bbc-a527-e9f4c9d178e9",
                                                "sense_id": "e95bf882-c189-3b0d-b750-d69f880c9de3",
                                                "text": "Welcome, we²l'ku²m. a.\n Received with gladneſs, admitted willingly, grateful[…]\nWelcome, we²l'ku²m. interj.\n A form of ſalutation uſed to a new comer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "823f98c9-336b-4c97-9c52-6f66b9e14d6b",
                                                "sense_id": "e95bf882-c189-3b0d-b750-d69f880c9de3",
                                                "text": "This new-comer was a man who in any company would have seemed striking. In complexion fair, and with blue or gray eyes, he was tall as any Viking, as broad in the shoulder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "410bf2d5-e73f-47a7-ab0f-fbd2bfe73dab",
                                                "sense_id": "e95bf882-c189-3b0d-b750-d69f880c9de3",
                                                "text": "As soon as Julia returned with a constable, Timothy, who was on the point of exhaustion, prepared to give over to him gratefully. The newcomer turned out to be a powerful youngster, fully trained and eager to help, and he stripped off his tunic at once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "035b5524-6597-4a2a-a295-95a53cd4d271",
                                                "sense_id": "e95bf882-c189-3b0d-b750-d69f880c9de3",
                                                "text": "Americans, for example, call newcomers to Antarctica “fingies”, which comes from FNGs – a borrowed military abbreviation that means “Fucking New Guy”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1fe83e4-e914-32fe-b066-398a61b19be7",
                                        "entry_id": "32ab7118-4cd3-3fd5-b7f8-e5ec8827d7ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A new participant in some activity; a neophyte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
